                "evidence": "On the Pro plan, LatticeCache 2.3 costs $45/month and caps a single item at 5 MB. The figures come from the vault page `wiki/LatticeCache.md`. It was reviewed 2026-11-04 against the official pricing and limits page, which was last updated 2026-11-02. The page is inside its 30-day freshness window, so I didn't search the web.\n\n**Cost:** $45/month base.\n\n**Included before overages start (per month):**\n- 20 GB of replicated NVMe cache storage\n- 50 million read ops\n- 10 million write ops\n\n**Overage rates beyond that:**\n- Storage: $1.80 per extra GB-month\n- Reads: $0.12 per million\n- Writes: $0.60 per million\n\n**Max item size:** 5 MB per value. The same page lists two other hard limits: keys up to 1,024 bytes, and 2,000 concurrent client connections per cache namespace.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The wiki page cites a raw capture (`raw/2026-11/2026-11-04 latticecache-2-3-pricing-limits`). It shows up in the vault listing, but two attempts to read it failed with \"No file\". I couldn't check the numbers against the original capture, so they rest on the compiled page alone.\n- Pricing pages change often, so re-check the official page before you commit to a budget.\n- Estimating your bill means working out your expected read and write volume against the 50M and 10M allowances. Writes run out first and cost five times as much per million as reads.\n\nI didn't write anything to the vault, since there was nothing new to add.\n\n**Coverage:**\n- Vault: read the guide, a search, and the `LatticeCache` page.\n- Raw source: listed but unreadable.\n- Web, social and subagent lanes: not searched, because the fresh vault page already answered the question.\n- Paid spend: none."
